WEBVTT

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:06.134
It's not as difficult
as it looks.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.605
The first rule is:

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.267
Don't be afraid of the clay.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.833
I fear nothing.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.435
I mean you can't
concern yourself

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.537
with making a mistake,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.309
or whether the image
you had in your mind

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.975
is what's taking form
in front of you.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.541
You just have
to let your hands...

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.746
and the clay... do the work.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.812
Here.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.995
Go ahead.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.996
I think the nose could be
a little stronger.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.997
Well, that's a start.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.031
Keep going.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.550
This activity
is truly unproductive.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.989
The end result has no use.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.493
No necessary task has been
accomplished.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.295
Time has been expended,
nothing more.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.856
That depends on how you
look at it, doesn't it?

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:11.735
I find sculpting
helps me unwind, relax.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.965
The concept of relaxation

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.701
is difficult for me
to understand.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.439
As a Borg, my time was spent
working at a specific task.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.606
When it was completed,
I was assigned another.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.309
It was efficient.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.646
Well, so is this.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.209
It helps my own efficiency

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.619
to forget about Voyager
for awhile.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.990
I'd be embarrassed
to show Maestro Leonardo

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:38.292
something like this, but...

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:42.734
I get a great deal of pleasure
in working the clay...

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.761
in creating something.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:49.707
But why here, in this simulation
among these archaic objects

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.869
and this disorganized
environment?

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.641
Frankly, it's refreshing
to take myself

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.707
out of the 24th century
every now and then.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.412
And a little disorganization

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:04.753
can be very encouraging
to the imagination.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.725
You might want to try it
sometime.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:11.423
Are you suggesting that I create
one of these holodeck programs?

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.694
You might find it interesting.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.827
It's a way of exploring
aspects of yourself

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:21.569
that probably didn't fit
into your life as a Borg...

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:22.597
imagination...

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.337
creativity...

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.639
fantasy...

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.442
I am uncertain why these things
are necessary.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.075
Well, they aren't necessary,
Seven,

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.642
but they're an important part
of one's life

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.120
because imagination
frees the mind,

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:39.125
it inspires ideas and solutions

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.651
and it can provide
a great deal of pleasure.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.595
Human progress...

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.258
the human mind itself

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.426
couldn't exist without them.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.993
When I was a child,
I studied these drawings.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.595
I even built
some of these models.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:58.200
Da Vinci was always
a great inspiration to me.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.836
He was a very busy man.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.814
Oh, yes, a prolific artist

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.477
and a scientist as well.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.009
Far, far ahead of his time.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.058
That design, for example.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.959
He conceived of an airplane

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.658
centuries before one
was actually built.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:20.859
Seven?

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.602
You will be assimilated.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.935
Resistance is futile.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:34.469
Your distinctiveness
will be added to our own.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:38.348
Annika!

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.478
You will be assimilated.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:44.012
You will be
assimilated.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.330
Seven, what is it?

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.796
I don't know.

00:05:53.951 --> 00:05:55.213
It's happened three times now

00:05:55.252 --> 00:05:57.686
in different locations,
at different times of the day.

00:05:57.721 --> 00:06:02.420
I experience a series
of disjointed images in my mind.

00:06:02.459 --> 00:06:04.484
Can you be more specific?

00:06:04.528 --> 00:06:06.894
Were these hallucinations?

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.364
I don't know.
I've never hallucinated.

00:06:09.399 --> 00:06:14.098
It's as if I were aboard
a Borg vessel, but...

00:06:14.138 --> 00:06:17.164
but I was frightened.
I felt fear.

00:06:19.977 --> 00:06:21.672
Each experience is similar...

00:06:21.712 --> 00:06:23.339
I'm pursued by the Borg.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.177
They want to assimilate me.

00:06:25.215 --> 00:06:29.083
I'm... I'm running from them,
and then...

00:06:29.119 --> 00:06:31.952
and then, each time,
I see... a bird.

00:06:32.022 --> 00:06:33.887
A bird?

00:06:33.924 --> 00:06:37.121
Yes, a large, black bird,
flying toward me,

00:06:37.161 --> 00:06:38.628
shrieking...

00:06:38.662 --> 00:06:40.289
attacking me.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.888
Hmm.

00:06:41.932 --> 00:06:44.162
Your hippocampus is
in a state of agitation.

00:06:44.201 --> 00:06:45.964
What does that mean?

00:06:46.003 --> 00:06:50.372
As your human physiology
continues to reassert itself,

00:06:50.407 --> 00:06:52.238
psychological symptoms
are bound to manifest

00:06:52.276 --> 00:06:53.641
in a variety of ways...

00:06:53.677 --> 00:06:56.441
through dreams, hallucinations,

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.471
hypnagogic regression...

00:06:58.515 --> 00:07:00.107
Hypnagogic regression?

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.447
Flashbacks.

00:07:01.485 --> 00:07:04.010
You could be experiencing
some sort of post-traumatic

00:07:04.054 --> 00:07:05.021
stress disorder.

00:07:05.055 --> 00:07:06.181
That makes sense.

00:07:06.223 --> 00:07:09.056
You were assimilated
by the Borg.

00:07:09.092 --> 00:07:11.890
You've gone through
an intense, prolonged trauma.

00:07:11.929 --> 00:07:13.556
I was not traumatized.

00:07:13.597 --> 00:07:15.462
I was raised by the Borg.

00:07:15.499 --> 00:07:17.399
I don't see them
as threatening.

00:07:17.434 --> 00:07:20.062
Why would I experience fear?

00:07:20.103 --> 00:07:21.671
I don't know.

00:07:21.804 --> 00:07:24.864
Will I keep having
these flashbacks?

00:07:24.907 --> 00:07:27.102
I'll need to study
your neural scans further.

00:07:27.143 --> 00:07:28.542
In the meantime,

00:07:28.577 --> 00:07:30.738
your digestive system
is fully functional.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.077
Now is as good a time as any

00:07:32.114 --> 00:07:34.708
for you to begin taking
solid and liquid nutrients.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.581
Oral consumption is inefficient.

00:07:36.619 --> 00:07:39.417
And unnecessary, if you're lucky
enough to be a hologram.

00:07:39.455 --> 00:07:41.889
But your human physiology
requires it.

00:07:41.924 --> 00:07:44.620
I'll draw up a list
of nutritional requirements.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.389
Take it to Mr. Neelix
in the Mess Hall.

00:07:46.429 --> 00:07:48.454
I hesitate to inflict
his cooking on you,

00:07:48.497 --> 00:07:50.658
but it'll have to do.

00:07:51.901 --> 00:07:54.631
I do not enjoy this sensation.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:57.696
Something is happening to me
and I don't know what it is.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.140
It's as though
I'm being driven somehow.

00:08:00.176 --> 00:08:01.609
Chakotay to the Captain.

00:08:01.644 --> 00:08:02.702
Go ahead.

00:08:02.745 --> 00:08:03.769
Our guests have arrived.

00:08:03.813 --> 00:08:05.405
They're being escorted
to the briefing room.

00:08:05.448 --> 00:08:06.574
On my way.

00:08:06.615 --> 00:08:07.912
Representatives of the B'omar.

00:08:07.983 --> 00:08:09.917
I've been trying to negotiate
passage through their space,

00:08:09.985 --> 00:08:11.919
but so far, they've been
difficult to deal with.

00:08:11.987 --> 00:08:13.921
I hope they've had
a change of heart.

00:08:13.956 --> 00:08:16.550
I'll stay here and wait for
the Doctor's instructions.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.128
We'll help you through this,
Seven.

00:08:20.162 --> 00:08:22.255
You'll be all right.

00:08:33.008 --> 00:08:35.636
Have you had a chance
to consider our request?

00:08:35.678 --> 00:08:37.236
Congratulations, Captain.

00:08:37.279 --> 00:08:40.043
Against our better judgment,
the B'omar Sovereignty

00:08:40.082 --> 00:08:41.947
has agreed to grant
your vessel passage

00:08:42.017 --> 00:08:43.382
through our territory.

00:08:43.419 --> 00:08:45.944
On behalf of my crew,
thank you.

00:08:46.055 --> 00:08:47.955
That will cut three months
off our journey.

00:08:48.057 --> 00:08:49.285
However, there are a few

00:08:49.325 --> 00:08:52.158
stipulations... guidelines
that you must adhere to.

00:08:52.194 --> 00:08:54.924
You'll have
our complete cooperation.

00:08:54.964 --> 00:08:57.091
We expect nothing less.

00:08:57.133 --> 00:09:00.728
While in our space, your vessel
will not exceed warp 3

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.829
and your weapon systems
will remain off-line.

00:09:02.872 --> 00:09:05.136
You will avoid unnecessary scans

00:09:05.174 --> 00:09:08.166
and you will not conduct
surveys of any kind.

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:10.474
You will make no attempt
to explore our space,

00:09:10.513 --> 00:09:12.378
and you will avoid
all communications

00:09:12.414 --> 00:09:13.608
with nonmilitary craft.

00:09:13.649 --> 00:09:16.584
We've also plotted the course
your vessel is to follow.

00:09:28.764 --> 00:09:30.755
It'll take us weeks
to follow that course.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.233
If not months.

00:09:32.268 --> 00:09:35.465
We've designed this course
so that your ship would avoid

00:09:35.504 --> 00:09:38.200
our populated systems
and industrial areas.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.301
Deviation is not recommended.

00:09:42.344 --> 00:09:44.244
There are a total
of 17 checkpoints

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.441
where you will submit
your vessel for inspection.

00:09:46.482 --> 00:09:49.144
Chancellor Gauman,
if I may interrupt.

00:09:49.185 --> 00:09:52.484
I appreciate your efforts
in plotting this flight plan,

00:09:52.521 --> 00:09:56.389
but, if we could, I'd like
to negotiate a course

00:09:56.425 --> 00:09:58.256
that's a little more...

00:09:58.294 --> 00:09:59.784
direct.

00:10:05.701 --> 00:10:08.226
Well,
what an unexpected pleasure.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.897
Welcome to the Mess Hall.

00:10:09.939 --> 00:10:12.703
Would you like me
to show you around?

00:10:12.741 --> 00:10:14.504
My physiology
has reasserted the need

00:10:14.543 --> 00:10:16.101
to process solid nutrients.

00:10:16.145 --> 00:10:18.875
The Doctor has prepared a list
of dietary requirements.

00:10:18.914 --> 00:10:20.313
You will provide them for me.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:22.874
Let's see what we have here.

00:10:22.918 --> 00:10:26.081
250 grams glycoproteins

00:10:26.121 --> 00:10:29.215
consisting of 53 percent
polypeptides

00:10:29.258 --> 00:10:32.716
and 26 percent
fibrous glycogen...

00:10:32.761 --> 00:10:34.092
Ugh!

00:10:34.129 --> 00:10:35.892
Doesn't sound very appetizing.

00:10:35.931 --> 00:10:38.593
However, a plate
of my chadre kab

00:10:38.634 --> 00:10:40.397
should satisfy
most of these essentials,

00:10:40.436 --> 00:10:43.564
while providing a pleasurable
culinary experience

00:10:43.606 --> 00:10:44.630
at the same time.

00:10:44.673 --> 00:10:46.140
Pleasure is irrelevant.

00:10:46.175 --> 00:10:47.665
Well, I beg to differ.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:50.838
A good meal involves much
more than simply providing

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.313
the proper nutrients.

00:10:52.348 --> 00:10:53.440
Why is that?

00:10:55.084 --> 00:10:57.143
Uh, well, it's a...

00:10:57.186 --> 00:10:59.780
There's a certain satisfaction
that comes from eating food

00:10:59.822 --> 00:11:01.255
that's been carefully prepared.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:03.485
I'm sure once you try it,
you'll understand.

00:11:03.525 --> 00:11:06.255
Now, how would you
like your chadre kab?

00:11:06.295 --> 00:11:07.853
Boiled? Baked?
Stir-fried?

00:11:07.897 --> 00:11:09.330
Preparation is irrelevant.

00:11:09.365 --> 00:11:10.627
Is irrelevant... maybe.

00:11:10.666 --> 00:11:11.963
Maybe not.

00:11:12.034 --> 00:11:14.502
This is the first time
ingesting food for you

00:11:14.536 --> 00:11:16.595
for quite awhile.

00:11:16.639 --> 00:11:18.539
We'll go a little easy
on your stomach...

00:11:18.574 --> 00:11:19.563
steamed.

00:11:22.611 --> 00:11:24.306
Yes...

00:11:24.346 --> 00:11:28.908
This, uh... this recipe
has been in my family

00:11:28.951 --> 00:11:30.441
for generations.

00:11:30.486 --> 00:11:32.454
It's considered a delicacy
among my people.

00:11:32.488 --> 00:11:34.513
You are Talaxian.

00:11:34.556 --> 00:11:36.649
Guilty as charged.

00:11:36.692 --> 00:11:38.125
Species 218.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.594
Well, I suppose so.

00:11:40.629 --> 00:11:42.221
Your biological
and technological

00:11:42.264 --> 00:11:44.061
distinctiveness
was added to our own.

00:11:46.869 --> 00:11:47.995
I hadn't realized that.

00:11:48.037 --> 00:11:50.232
A small freighter,
containing a crew of 39,

00:11:50.272 --> 00:11:51.899
taken in the Dalmine Sector.

00:11:51.941 --> 00:11:54.637
They were easily assimilated.

00:11:54.677 --> 00:11:57.612
Their dense musculature
made them excellent drones.

00:11:58.747 --> 00:12:01.511
Well... lucky for you, I guess.

00:12:05.254 --> 00:12:06.653
Your nutrients.

00:12:10.793 --> 00:12:12.055
Follow me.

00:12:27.009 --> 00:12:28.601
Please.

00:12:28.644 --> 00:12:30.305
Please what?

00:12:30.346 --> 00:12:32.871
It's customary to sit
while eating.

00:12:45.361 --> 00:12:48.159
Uh, is something wrong?

00:12:48.197 --> 00:12:50.688
I am unaccustomed to this.

00:12:50.733 --> 00:12:52.462
Borg do not sit.

00:12:52.501 --> 00:12:55.937
Well, this is a day of firsts,
then, isn't it?

00:12:58.807 --> 00:13:00.365
Now...

00:13:02.011 --> 00:13:03.569
take a bite.

00:13:05.347 --> 00:13:07.338
Uh... try that one.

00:13:10.486 --> 00:13:12.249
Just kind of, uh...

00:13:12.287 --> 00:13:13.652
scoop some up.

00:13:16.125 --> 00:13:17.456
That's the way.

00:13:17.493 --> 00:13:18.960
Right into your mouth,

00:13:19.028 --> 00:13:22.395
just like a little scout ship
flying into a shuttle bay.

00:13:25.467 --> 00:13:26.866
Take it out.

00:13:26.902 --> 00:13:27.926
Keep your mouth closed.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.562
That's right.

00:13:31.573 --> 00:13:32.540
Now, you chew...

00:13:32.574 --> 00:13:33.734
chew, chew, chew, chew, chew.

00:13:36.345 --> 00:13:38.279
And swallow.

00:13:40.916 --> 00:13:43.180
Uh, swallow. Uh...

00:13:52.895 --> 00:13:54.726
Curious sensation.

00:13:54.763 --> 00:13:55.889
You'll get used to it.

00:13:55.931 --> 00:13:57.523
Have some more.

00:14:12.047 --> 00:14:15.039
May I bring you something else?

00:14:16.118 --> 00:14:18.643
A soothing cup of tea,
perhaps?

00:14:34.402 --> 00:14:37.303
You will be assimilated.

00:14:37.338 --> 00:14:39.568
Resistance is futile.

00:14:43.311 --> 00:14:45.108
Did you see that?

00:14:55.089 --> 00:14:56.954
What about this course?

00:14:56.991 --> 00:14:58.424
It's a marginal adjustment.

00:14:58.459 --> 00:14:59.687
The nearest populated system

00:14:59.727 --> 00:15:01.354
is more than three
light-years away.

00:15:01.396 --> 00:15:03.023
Definitely not.

00:15:03.064 --> 00:15:06.158
You'd pass directly through
the Agrat-Mot Nebula,

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.600
a key resource
in our trade negotiations

00:15:08.636 --> 00:15:09.796
with the Nassordin.

00:15:09.837 --> 00:15:11.236
I could chart the nebula

00:15:11.272 --> 00:15:12.933
- try to avoid...
- No, no.

00:15:12.974 --> 00:15:16.535
Are your translators
malfunctioning?

00:15:16.577 --> 00:15:18.943
Captain Janeway to the Bridge.

00:15:19.013 --> 00:15:20.241
If you'll excuse me.

00:15:23.584 --> 00:15:24.949
Report.

00:15:25.053 --> 00:15:26.884
I've received
an alert from Security.

00:15:26.921 --> 00:15:29.151
Seven of Nine attacked
Neelix in the Mess Hall

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.215
and three other crewmen
on Deck 2.

00:15:31.259 --> 00:15:32.954
Janeway to Seven of Nine.

00:15:32.994 --> 00:15:36.054
Seven, if you can hear me,
respond.

00:15:36.097 --> 00:15:37.621
What's her location?

00:15:37.665 --> 00:15:40.099
Deck 6, Section 28-Alpha.

00:15:40.134 --> 00:15:41.294
Take a security team.

00:15:43.004 --> 00:15:44.437
Captain...

00:15:44.472 --> 00:15:45.530
what is happening here?

00:15:45.573 --> 00:15:46.801
I wish I knew, Chancellor.

00:15:46.841 --> 00:15:49.139
Chakotay, seal off Deck 6.

00:15:52.547 --> 00:15:54.174
Seven of Nine.

00:16:13.267 --> 00:16:15.758
Security to Captain Janeway.

00:16:15.803 --> 00:16:17.668
We've just seen Seven of Nine.

00:16:17.705 --> 00:16:19.400
Her Borg shields
are fully operational

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.930
and they've adapted
to our phasers.

00:16:21.008 --> 00:16:22.942
Acknowledged.

00:16:23.044 --> 00:16:25.706
Bridge to all
security personnel.

00:16:25.747 --> 00:16:29.148
Configure your weapons
to a rotating modulation,

00:16:29.183 --> 00:16:31.174
but keep them on "stun."

00:16:31.219 --> 00:16:32.243
Borg?

00:16:32.286 --> 00:16:34.345
You have Borg on your ship?

00:16:34.389 --> 00:16:35.651
It's not what you think.

00:16:35.690 --> 00:16:37.157
She is a member of my crew.

00:16:37.191 --> 00:16:39.125
We liberated her
from the collective.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.422
She's no longer a Borg.

00:16:40.461 --> 00:16:42.588
Then why is she equipped
with Borg shields?

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:43.790
I don't know.

00:16:50.671 --> 00:16:53.071
She's able to cross
through the security fields.

00:16:53.107 --> 00:16:55.268
She's entering
the armory on Deck 6.

00:17:02.817 --> 00:17:04.284
Deck 10.

00:17:06.254 --> 00:17:07.243
She's in a turbolift.

00:17:07.288 --> 00:17:08.880
Cut power to the turboshafts.

00:17:08.923 --> 00:17:11.687
She's blocking my commands
with a Borg encryption code.

00:17:11.726 --> 00:17:12.750
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:17:12.794 --> 00:17:14.284
Seven's apparently
headed for Deck 10.

00:17:14.328 --> 00:17:15.920
Can you get there
before she does?

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:18.225
I'm moving into position
now, Captain.

00:17:19.867 --> 00:17:21.425
We'll take position here.

00:17:35.016 --> 00:17:37.985
Lower your weapon
and stand down.

00:17:40.855 --> 00:17:42.584
Fire.

00:17:52.099 --> 00:17:53.464
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:17:53.501 --> 00:17:54.934
We were unsuccessful.

00:17:56.037 --> 00:17:57.470
I have wounded.

00:17:57.505 --> 00:17:59.200
She's moving toward
Junction 32-Alpha.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:00.867
The Shuttle Bay.

00:18:00.908 --> 00:18:02.899
I'm erecting a force field.

00:18:02.944 --> 00:18:05.742
Harry, reroute all
available power to Deck 10.

00:18:06.781 --> 00:18:08.112
Done.

00:18:20.394 --> 00:18:22.362
She's accessing
transporter control.

00:18:29.437 --> 00:18:31.598
She used
a site-to-site transport.

00:18:31.639 --> 00:18:34.301
She's in a shuttlecraft...

00:18:34.342 --> 00:18:35.639
powering engines.

00:18:35.676 --> 00:18:36.734
Seal the launch doors.

00:18:41.349 --> 00:18:42.441
Tractor beam!

00:18:42.483 --> 00:18:43.848
No effect.

00:18:43.885 --> 00:18:46.376
She's remodulated
the shuttle's shield harmonics.

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:48.445
Captain.

00:18:48.489 --> 00:18:50.548
Seven's headed directly
into B'omar space.

00:18:50.591 --> 00:18:51.956
She's gone to warp.

00:18:51.993 --> 00:18:53.620
She's masked
the shuttle's ion trail.

00:18:53.661 --> 00:18:54.753
I've lost her signal.

00:18:54.795 --> 00:18:56.558
She's gone.

00:19:08.376 --> 00:19:10.071
We'll do everything in our power
to find her,

00:19:10.111 --> 00:19:12.636
but we will need permission
to enter B'omar space

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.477
to track her shuttle
effectively.

00:19:14.515 --> 00:19:17.245
Let's tally the events,
shall we?

00:19:17.285 --> 00:19:20.015
First, you arrive
uninvited and unwelcome,

00:19:20.054 --> 00:19:22.488
requesting a shortcut
through our space.

00:19:22.523 --> 00:19:25.048
Then you proceed to unleash
some sort of rogue Borg

00:19:25.092 --> 00:19:28.118
and now you want us to help you
get it back.

00:19:28.162 --> 00:19:29.857
I apologize
for what's happened here,

00:19:29.897 --> 00:19:32.695
but we certainly didn't
"unleash" anyone.

00:19:32.733 --> 00:19:35.497
We can resolve this situation
quickly, gentlemen,

00:19:35.536 --> 00:19:36.935
if we work together.

00:19:36.971 --> 00:19:39.565
Captain Janeway,
after what I've seen here,

00:19:39.607 --> 00:19:41.837
I question your competence.

00:19:41.876 --> 00:19:44.470
May I remind you
that you're still on my ship.

00:19:44.512 --> 00:19:49.415
And you are only one vessel
among many of ours.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:53.546
Your Borg will be dealt with
quickly and efficiently.

00:19:53.588 --> 00:19:55.317
It's being tracked as we speak.

00:19:55.356 --> 00:19:57.415
Tracked... how?

00:19:57.458 --> 00:20:00.291
Every vessel, every object,

00:20:00.328 --> 00:20:04.458
every particle of dust
that crosses our borders

00:20:04.498 --> 00:20:07.399
is immediately identified
and traced

00:20:07.435 --> 00:20:09.426
by our perimeter grid.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.631
The Borg will be found...
and destroyed.

00:20:11.672 --> 00:20:12.639
Chancellor...

00:20:12.673 --> 00:20:14.607
There will be no sharing
of information.

00:20:14.642 --> 00:20:15.609
From this point on,

00:20:15.643 --> 00:20:17.270
your vessel
will maintain a distance

00:20:17.311 --> 00:20:19.609
of at least five light-years
from our borders.

00:20:19.647 --> 00:20:21.581
Any deviation

00:20:21.616 --> 00:20:23.982
will be considered
an act of aggression.

00:20:25.853 --> 00:20:28.185
Commander,

00:20:28.222 --> 00:20:30.850
escort our guests
to the transporter room.

00:20:38.899 --> 00:20:41.459
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:20:41.502 --> 00:20:42.901
I've assembled a team

00:20:42.937 --> 00:20:46.168
to analyze every square meter
of the cargo bay.

00:20:46.207 --> 00:20:48.075
This has essentially been
her quarters

00:20:48.208 --> 00:20:49.732
for the past two months.

00:20:49.776 --> 00:20:52.142
I'm determined
to find something here

00:20:52.179 --> 00:20:55.307
that might shed some light
on Seven of Nine's actions.

00:21:05.992 --> 00:21:07.960
You're taking this kind
of hard, aren't you?

00:21:08.028 --> 00:21:09.928
What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:13.533 --> 00:21:15.558
We had a working relationship.

00:21:15.602 --> 00:21:19.094
Well, what's that
supposed to mean?

00:21:19.139 --> 00:21:21.505
It's not what you're thinking.

00:21:21.541 --> 00:21:24.374
What am I thinking, Harry?

00:21:24.411 --> 00:21:26.538
Never mind.

00:21:45.732 --> 00:21:47.495
Take a look at this.

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:55.139
Anything?

00:21:55.175 --> 00:21:56.767
It's a Borg data-link.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:59.745
It contains a succession
of log entries

00:21:59.779 --> 00:22:01.872
written in Borg
alphanumeric code.

00:22:01.915 --> 00:22:03.849
I'm getting pretty good
with the Borg language.

00:22:03.884 --> 00:22:05.146
I think I can translate them.

00:22:05.185 --> 00:22:06.209
Get on it.

00:22:07.888 --> 00:22:10.584
It seems we've made quite
an impression on the B'omar.

00:22:10.624 --> 00:22:12.956
In the last hour, they've
doubled the number of ships

00:22:13.026 --> 00:22:14.323
patrolling their borders,

00:22:14.361 --> 00:22:16.056
and they've increased
the sensitivity

00:22:16.096 --> 00:22:17.757
of the perimeter
grid by 36 percent.

00:22:17.797 --> 00:22:19.094
So much for diplomacy.

00:22:19.132 --> 00:22:20.565
The Doctor analyzed the data

00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:22.534
from Seven of Nine's
last transport.

00:22:22.569 --> 00:22:24.332
He's found something
he wants us to see.

00:22:26.039 --> 00:22:27.836
Maybe this was inevitable.

00:22:27.874 --> 00:22:29.739
Even if Seven did want
to stay on Voyager,

00:22:29.776 --> 00:22:31.710
her Borg nature
may have won out.

00:22:31.745 --> 00:22:33.736
We can remove implant
after implant,

00:22:33.780 --> 00:22:36.806
but maybe at her core,

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:38.977
she'll always be part
of the collective.

00:22:39.019 --> 00:22:40.646
No. I won't accept that.

00:22:42.822 --> 00:22:44.312
Deck 5.

00:22:44.357 --> 00:22:47.087
She was responding to us...

00:22:47.127 --> 00:22:49.687
interacting with people
outside of the collective

00:22:49.729 --> 00:22:50.753
for the first time.

00:22:50.797 --> 00:22:52.890
She was adapting
to this environment

00:22:52.933 --> 00:22:54.696
and to this crew.

00:22:54.734 --> 00:22:56.224
But where is she going?

00:22:56.269 --> 00:22:58.328
We've scanned space

00:22:58.371 --> 00:22:59.998
for a distance
of 40 light-years.

00:23:00.073 --> 00:23:02.200
We've found no evidence
of Borg ships,

00:23:02.242 --> 00:23:03.937
so she can't be trying
to rejoin the collective.

00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:06.274
She may plan to take the
shuttle back to Borg space.

00:23:06.313 --> 00:23:07.712
10,000 light-years from here?

00:23:07.747 --> 00:23:08.805
I don't think so.
No.

00:23:08.848 --> 00:23:10.509
Something else is going on.

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:13.951
We're missing a piece
of the puzzle.

00:23:14.054 --> 00:23:15.612
In the meantime,
the B'omar intend

00:23:15.655 --> 00:23:19.056
to find her, and if they do,
she'll probably resist them.

00:23:19.092 --> 00:23:21.458
One more reason
for us to find her first.

00:23:26.399 --> 00:23:27.764
What have you found, Doctor?

00:23:27.801 --> 00:23:29.496
Something most peculiar.

00:23:29.536 --> 00:23:31.800
This graphic represents
the matter conversion data

00:23:31.838 --> 00:23:33.430
from Seven of Nine's
last transport.

00:23:33.473 --> 00:23:34.497
If you'll notice,

00:23:34.541 --> 00:23:36.771
there's a high concentration
of Borg organelles

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.370
in the bone marrow
and lymphatic tissue.

00:23:39.412 --> 00:23:41.972
The dormant nanoprobes
in Seven of Nine's cells

00:23:42.015 --> 00:23:43.209
have reasserted themselves.

00:23:43.250 --> 00:23:44.842
Taken over blood cell
production,

00:23:44.884 --> 00:23:47.284
and they're growing
new Borg implants.

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:48.981
13 percent
of the Borg technology

00:23:49.089 --> 00:23:50.454
I removed three weeks ago

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:52.583
has regenerated
in a matter of hours.

00:23:52.626 --> 00:23:55.390
You said the nanoprobes in
her bloodstream were dormant.

00:23:55.428 --> 00:23:56.520
What reactivated them?

00:23:56.563 --> 00:23:57.996
I don't know.

00:23:58.064 --> 00:24:00.828
But I've developed a way
to stop the process.

00:24:00.867 --> 00:24:03.665
This hypospray contains
a genetic resequencing vector.

00:24:03.703 --> 00:24:05.830
It should neutralize
the nanoprobes.

00:24:05.872 --> 00:24:08.238
That means someone needs
to get close enough to do it.

00:24:14.214 --> 00:24:15.579
Report.

00:24:15.615 --> 00:24:17.742
We've analyzed
the B'omar perimeter grid.

00:24:17.784 --> 00:24:18.944
It's sophisticated,

00:24:19.019 --> 00:24:21.112
but not without
its vulnerabilities.

00:24:21.154 --> 00:24:23.349
It might be possible
to penetrate the grid

00:24:23.390 --> 00:24:25.790
by recalibrating our shields
to match its frequency.

00:24:25.825 --> 00:24:28.726
The trick is going to be
our energy signature.

00:24:28.762 --> 00:24:29.888
Voyager's too big to hide,

00:24:29.929 --> 00:24:32.693
but a shuttlecraft with
the proper shield modulation

00:24:32.732 --> 00:24:34.165
and its engines powered down

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:36.930
could drift right through
without so much as a peep.

00:24:36.970 --> 00:24:39.962
Nice work, gentlemen.
Proceed.

00:24:40.073 --> 00:24:42.974
The Doctor's genetic resequencer
should keep her sedated

00:24:43.009 --> 00:24:45.068
until you get back
to the ship.

00:24:45.111 --> 00:24:46.976
Once you've penetrated
the perimeter,

00:24:47.013 --> 00:24:49.982
there will be no further
communication with Voyager.

00:24:50.016 --> 00:24:51.381
You'll be on your own.

00:24:51.418 --> 00:24:53.477
Captain, it is possible

00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:55.715
that Seven will adapt
to the resequencer.

00:24:55.755 --> 00:24:56.983
I know.

00:24:57.023 --> 00:25:02.655
If it fails and you're unable
to reason with her...

00:25:02.696 --> 00:25:05.688
you have my authorization
to stop her...

00:25:05.732 --> 00:25:07.757
with any force necessary.

00:25:10.103 --> 00:25:11.161
Understood.

00:25:20.980 --> 00:25:25.349
Seven of Nine, grid nine-two
of subjunction 12.

00:25:26.619 --> 00:25:28.246
You will be assimilated.

00:25:45.939 --> 00:25:47.736
Borg drone, you have committed

00:25:47.774 --> 00:25:51.266
an infraction
against the B'omar Sovereignty.

00:25:52.379 --> 00:25:56.440
Cut power to your engines
and lower your shields.

00:25:56.483 --> 00:25:58.610
Prepare to be boarded.

00:25:59.819 --> 00:26:02.913
You will proceed no further.

00:26:02.956 --> 00:26:03.945
We will not...

00:26:12.065 --> 00:26:14.556
I'm detecting
weapon signatures...

00:26:14.601 --> 00:26:17.069
Federation and B'omar.

00:26:17.103 --> 00:26:21.199
Five B'omar vessels
are adrift... heavily damaged.

00:26:21.241 --> 00:26:23.334
Life signs are stable.

00:26:23.376 --> 00:26:24.934
I've located Seven's shuttle.

00:26:25.044 --> 00:26:27.774
It's 2.5 million
kilometers from here.

00:26:27.814 --> 00:26:29.179
Adjust course to intercept.

00:26:36.089 --> 00:26:37.681
The implants in Seven's body

00:26:37.724 --> 00:26:38.952
are disrupting
the transporter signal.

00:26:39.058 --> 00:26:40.548
I can't get a lock.

00:26:40.593 --> 00:26:42.754
See if you can remodulate
our transporters

00:26:42.796 --> 00:26:44.354
to match her shields.

00:26:44.397 --> 00:26:46.729
You want to beam in there?

00:26:46.766 --> 00:26:48.734
Yes.

00:26:48.768 --> 00:26:51.464
I don't think
that's such a good idea, Tuvok.

00:26:51.504 --> 00:26:53.904
Close quarters...
Borg against Vulcan.

00:26:53.940 --> 00:26:55.965
No offense, but you
don't stand a chance

00:26:56.009 --> 00:26:57.704
if she decides
to put up a fight.

00:26:57.744 --> 00:26:59.769
It's my hope
that the element of surprise

00:26:59.813 --> 00:27:00.973
will work in my favor.

00:27:02.348 --> 00:27:04.179
Do you have a better idea?

00:27:06.319 --> 00:27:08.344
Come to think of it, no.

00:27:11.090 --> 00:27:12.614
She's charging weapons.

00:27:12.659 --> 00:27:15.184
Set my coordinates
for the aft compartment.

00:27:15.228 --> 00:27:16.490
Ready.

00:27:16.529 --> 00:27:18.019
Energize.

00:27:34.481 --> 00:27:38.747
Come on, Tuvok.
Give me a sign.

00:27:47.126 --> 00:27:50.459
Warning. Propulsion systems
are off-line.

00:27:50.497 --> 00:27:51.930
Damn!

00:28:11.416 --> 00:28:14.044
That's a level-5 force field,
Lieutenant.

00:28:14.085 --> 00:28:16.019
I suggest you be more careful.

00:28:16.054 --> 00:28:18.420
Why have you left Voyager?

00:28:20.158 --> 00:28:22.183
I am Borg.

00:28:22.226 --> 00:28:25.627
You were Borg...
but you're human now.

00:28:25.663 --> 00:28:27.563
You are part of our crew.

00:28:32.236 --> 00:28:35.535
For a brief time, I was human.

00:28:35.573 --> 00:28:39.805
But I have come to realize
that I am Borg.

00:28:39.844 --> 00:28:42.938
I will always be Borg.

00:28:43.014 --> 00:28:45.482
What prompted this realization?

00:28:45.516 --> 00:28:49.714
Every Borg ship is coded to emit
a distinct resonance frequency

00:28:49.754 --> 00:28:53.087
to guide drones who have become
separated from the collective.

00:28:53.124 --> 00:28:54.648
A homing beacon.

00:28:54.692 --> 00:28:56.922
Yes.

00:28:56.961 --> 00:28:58.952
I am following a signal.

00:28:59.030 --> 00:29:02.693
A Borg vessel is waiting for me.

00:29:02.734 --> 00:29:05.760
We've scanned this entire region
for Borg.

00:29:05.803 --> 00:29:07.668
There are none.

00:29:07.705 --> 00:29:09.229
You're wrong.

00:29:11.576 --> 00:29:12.907
They are here.

00:29:19.817 --> 00:29:21.375
Vulcan.

00:29:21.419 --> 00:29:24.081
Species 3259.

00:29:24.122 --> 00:29:25.680
Your enlarged neocortex

00:29:25.723 --> 00:29:28.385
produces superior
analytical abilities.

00:29:28.426 --> 00:29:31.088
Your distinctiveness
will be added to our...

00:29:33.531 --> 00:29:34.896
Seven?

00:29:40.371 --> 00:29:41.736
No.

00:29:46.077 --> 00:29:48.045
I will not assimilate you.

00:29:50.782 --> 00:29:52.409
Once I have returned
to the collective,

00:29:52.450 --> 00:29:54.315
you will go back to Voyager

00:29:54.352 --> 00:29:56.718
and tell Captain Janeway
what's happened to me.

00:29:58.556 --> 00:30:03.960
Thank her for her patience...
for her kindness.

00:30:04.062 --> 00:30:06.428
Curious.

00:30:06.464 --> 00:30:12.266
Your behavior demonstrates
affection and sentiment.

00:30:12.303 --> 00:30:15.761
Traits of humanity...
hardly Borg.

00:30:18.609 --> 00:30:22.602
You have been experiencing
hallucinations, flashbacks?

00:30:22.647 --> 00:30:24.274
Yes.

00:30:24.315 --> 00:30:25.714
Does that usually occur

00:30:25.750 --> 00:30:28.014
when a resonance signal
is activated?

00:30:30.154 --> 00:30:31.587
No.

00:30:31.622 --> 00:30:36.992
Seven of Nine, grid nine-two
of subjunction 12.

00:30:37.061 --> 00:30:41.896
But I can hear them...
calling me.

00:30:41.933 --> 00:30:44.561
I'm frightened.

00:30:44.602 --> 00:30:46.126
That's understandable.

00:30:46.170 --> 00:30:48.934
Lower the force field.

00:30:48.973 --> 00:30:50.736
We can return to Voyager

00:30:50.775 --> 00:30:53.471
and find out
what's happening to you.

00:30:53.511 --> 00:30:55.570
I am your shipmate.

00:30:55.613 --> 00:30:58.741
We can return to Voyager
together.

00:31:01.119 --> 00:31:03.781
I must rejoin the collective.

00:31:09.627 --> 00:31:11.891
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:31:11.929 --> 00:31:15.228
I've been trying to retrace
Seven of Nine's footsteps...

00:31:15.266 --> 00:31:17.632
her actions
during the last few days,

00:31:17.668 --> 00:31:19.101
but I'm still no closer

00:31:19.137 --> 00:31:21.037
to understanding
what's happened.

00:31:26.644 --> 00:31:27.611
Captain?

00:31:27.645 --> 00:31:29.272
Am I disturbing you?

00:31:29.313 --> 00:31:31.747
Not at all, Harry.

00:31:31.782 --> 00:31:34.808
I've managed to decipher
Seven's log entries.

00:31:36.487 --> 00:31:38.648
And?

00:31:38.689 --> 00:31:39.849
There's nothing that indicates

00:31:39.891 --> 00:31:41.290
she was planning
to leave the ship.

00:31:41.325 --> 00:31:43.657
The entries are
pretty unremarkable.

00:31:43.694 --> 00:31:45.355
She describes
her daily routines

00:31:45.396 --> 00:31:47.330
the number of hours
spent regenerating,

00:31:47.365 --> 00:31:48.332
that sort of thing.

00:31:48.366 --> 00:31:50.163
There were
some personal log entries,

00:31:50.201 --> 00:31:52.829
mostly observations
about the crew's behavior.

00:31:52.870 --> 00:31:55.338
I'm mentioned
in quite a few of them.

00:31:55.373 --> 00:31:59.366
Apparently, she finds
my behavior easy to predict,

00:31:59.410 --> 00:32:00.377
whatever that means.

00:32:00.411 --> 00:32:01.673
Don't take it personally.

00:32:01.712 --> 00:32:04.613
Coming from Seven,
that's probably a compliment.

00:32:06.384 --> 00:32:09.080
Uh, the most recent entries
are kind of strange.

00:32:11.222 --> 00:32:13.053
Descriptions of bizarre images,

00:32:13.090 --> 00:32:14.853
almost like a record
of her dreams.

00:32:14.892 --> 00:32:15.881
The hallucinations?

00:32:15.927 --> 00:32:17.087
Maybe so.

00:32:17.128 --> 00:32:19.494
Sometimes she's in a Borg vessel

00:32:19.530 --> 00:32:21.930
running... or hiding
behind a bulkhead,

00:32:21.966 --> 00:32:23.297
falling down a shaft.

00:32:23.334 --> 00:32:25.302
Borg everywhere, chasing her.

00:32:25.336 --> 00:32:26.462
Nightmarish stuff.

00:32:26.504 --> 00:32:28.267
What about this... bird?

00:32:28.306 --> 00:32:30.137
She mentions it several times.

00:32:30.174 --> 00:32:32.199
It flies at her, shrieking.

00:32:32.243 --> 00:32:33.574
I don't know what it means.

00:32:33.611 --> 00:32:35.340
"The feathers are black.

00:32:35.379 --> 00:32:38.280
"Wingspan approximately
one half meter.

00:32:38.316 --> 00:32:40.375
"The eyes are yellow

00:32:40.418 --> 00:32:43.478
"and it has a powerful
triangular beak.

00:32:43.521 --> 00:32:44.886
When it looks at me..."

00:32:46.691 --> 00:32:48.989
"I am paralyzed.

00:32:49.026 --> 00:32:51.756
"I cannot move.

00:32:51.796 --> 00:32:54.629
"It seems to know me,

00:32:54.665 --> 00:32:58.465
"but I don't understand
how that's possible.

00:32:58.502 --> 00:33:04.168
"It's merely a bird,
an inferior form of life,

00:33:04.208 --> 00:33:09.236
but the sight of it
fills me with fear."

00:33:09.280 --> 00:33:12.738
It sounds like she's describing
a member of the...

00:33:12.783 --> 00:33:15.877
Corvidae family, like a crow
or...

00:33:20.625 --> 00:33:22.456
Or a raven.

00:33:24.795 --> 00:33:27.320
She's describing a raven.

00:33:27.365 --> 00:33:29.458
Why is that important?

00:33:29.500 --> 00:33:31.934
Because now I know
what to look for.

00:33:35.306 --> 00:33:38.207
Chakotay, calibrate
our long-range sensors

00:33:38.242 --> 00:33:40.472
to scan for
any Federation signature

00:33:40.511 --> 00:33:41.978
other than our two shuttlecraft.

00:33:42.013 --> 00:33:43.480
- Captain?
- Do it.

00:33:43.514 --> 00:33:44.981
Bring the ship about, Ensign,

00:33:45.082 --> 00:33:48.108
and lay in a course
for B'omar space.

00:33:48.152 --> 00:33:49.312
Aye, Captain.

00:34:01.632 --> 00:34:04.533
The resonance signal is coming
from the lunar surface.

00:34:07.905 --> 00:34:10.271
The Borg are waiting
for me there.

00:34:12.810 --> 00:34:14.368
I don't know why I'm frightened.

00:34:14.412 --> 00:34:15.401
They are my people.

00:34:15.446 --> 00:34:19.075
If you are afraid,
then leave this place.

00:34:19.116 --> 00:34:21.311
Once I have been reintegrated
into the collective,

00:34:21.352 --> 00:34:22.842
my fears will disappear.

00:34:24.955 --> 00:34:26.752
Deactivate the force field.

00:34:26.791 --> 00:34:29.783
I will accompany you
to the surface.

00:34:29.827 --> 00:34:31.488
You don't need to go alone.

00:34:35.232 --> 00:34:37.393
You would be assimilated.

00:34:37.435 --> 00:34:39.460
I don't believe so.

00:34:39.503 --> 00:34:41.903
I think the situation
is not what it appears.

00:34:41.939 --> 00:34:43.873
What do you mean?
What else could it be?

00:34:43.908 --> 00:34:45.876
I am uncertain,
but I am willing

00:34:45.910 --> 00:34:48.538
to go with you to the surface
to find out.

00:34:58.922 --> 00:35:00.321
Voyager to Paris.

00:35:00.357 --> 00:35:02.086
Paris here, Captain.

00:35:02.125 --> 00:35:04.059
Glad to hear your voice.

00:35:04.094 --> 00:35:06.187
Tuvok is with Seven of Nine.

00:35:06.229 --> 00:35:08.697
I haven't been able to establish
communication with him

00:35:08.732 --> 00:35:11.292
since he transported
to her shuttle.

00:35:11.334 --> 00:35:14.064
I've tracked them
to an M-Class moon

00:35:14.104 --> 00:35:16.868
orbiting the fifth planet
of a yellow dwarf star.

00:35:16.906 --> 00:35:19.204
I'm picking up
an unusual resonance signal

00:35:19.242 --> 00:35:20.402
from the surface.

00:35:20.443 --> 00:35:21.410
It's erratic.

00:35:21.444 --> 00:35:23.105
I haven't been able
to identify it.

00:35:23.146 --> 00:35:24.909
Acknowledged.

00:35:24.948 --> 00:35:26.745
We've detected
several B'omar ships

00:35:26.783 --> 00:35:28.580
closing in on your position.

00:35:28.618 --> 00:35:30.449
What's your condition?

00:35:30.487 --> 00:35:31.647
Warp engines are off-line.

00:35:31.688 --> 00:35:33.849
Shields are at 50 percent.

00:35:33.890 --> 00:35:35.448
Try to locate them, Tom.

00:35:35.492 --> 00:35:36.618
We're on our way.

00:35:43.533 --> 00:35:45.228
The signal's getting stronger.

00:35:45.268 --> 00:35:46.895
They're here.
I'm sure of it.

00:35:46.936 --> 00:35:48.528
This way.

00:35:53.476 --> 00:35:56.036
If you wish, we can return
to the shuttle.

00:35:58.982 --> 00:36:01.143
No. I have to find out.

00:36:13.063 --> 00:36:14.360
What is it?

00:36:14.397 --> 00:36:16.331
It's a Federation vessel

00:36:16.366 --> 00:36:18.732
partially assimilated
by the Borg.

00:36:18.768 --> 00:36:20.895
There are no life signs.

00:36:20.937 --> 00:36:21.926
Tritanium decay

00:36:22.005 --> 00:36:24.974
suggests it has been here
for nearly 20 years.

00:36:42.358 --> 00:36:44.087
This vessel is familiar.

00:37:00.210 --> 00:37:02.269
This is the signal
that's drawn me here.

00:37:10.220 --> 00:37:13.189
Annika!

00:37:13.223 --> 00:37:17.489
Run, Annika!

00:37:17.527 --> 00:37:19.893
Run! Hide!

00:37:28.171 --> 00:37:29.297
Papa?

00:37:30.840 --> 00:37:32.205
Help me.

00:37:41.151 --> 00:37:44.279
No! No!

00:37:45.822 --> 00:37:48.313
Seven, I'm here.

00:37:48.358 --> 00:37:49.882
Listen to me.

00:37:54.531 --> 00:37:55.759
Come.

00:38:10.346 --> 00:38:12.837
It happened here.

00:38:14.417 --> 00:38:15.748
This is where it began.

00:38:15.785 --> 00:38:17.616
This is where I was assimilated.

00:38:29.666 --> 00:38:31.657
This was our ship.

00:38:34.704 --> 00:38:36.035
We lived here.

00:38:37.974 --> 00:38:40.306
We lived here for a long time.

00:38:44.647 --> 00:38:46.376
My father did experiments.

00:38:46.416 --> 00:38:48.281
They were very important

00:38:48.318 --> 00:38:50.809
and we had to travel
a long way.

00:38:54.624 --> 00:38:56.421
I had my birthday here.

00:38:59.162 --> 00:39:01.790
My cake had
six candles on it and...

00:39:03.766 --> 00:39:05.927
and one more to grow on.

00:39:09.939 --> 00:39:11.531
And then the men came.

00:39:14.744 --> 00:39:18.077
Papa tried to fight them,
but they were too strong.

00:39:20.116 --> 00:39:21.481
I tried to hide.

00:39:23.253 --> 00:39:26.450
Maybe they wouldn't find me
because I was little.

00:39:26.489 --> 00:39:29.287
But they did.

00:39:32.495 --> 00:39:34.429
And then Papa said
we were going to crash

00:39:34.464 --> 00:39:37.900
and... the big man
picked me up...

00:39:39.736 --> 00:39:42.102
and then suddenly,
we weren't on this ship anymore.

00:39:42.138 --> 00:39:43.264
We were somewhere else.

00:39:48.945 --> 00:39:51.539
And then I became Borg.

00:39:53.916 --> 00:39:55.781
Fascinating.

00:39:55.818 --> 00:39:57.285
This resonance signal
must have been active

00:39:57.320 --> 00:40:01.279
since the ship was assimilated
and Voyager passed within range.

00:40:03.159 --> 00:40:05.184
The ship is under attack.

00:40:05.228 --> 00:40:06.820
The B'omar.

00:40:07.430 --> 00:40:08.863
The ship will collapse.

00:40:08.898 --> 00:40:09.990
We must get out of here.

00:40:22.879 --> 00:40:25.279
The B'omar still aren't
responding to our hails.

00:40:25.315 --> 00:40:26.782
Standing by to fire.

00:40:26.816 --> 00:40:28.579
Target their weapon systems.

00:40:28.618 --> 00:40:30.984
Tom, what's your status?

00:40:31.054 --> 00:40:32.146
I've located Tuvok and Seven,

00:40:32.188 --> 00:40:33.553
but there's a lot
of interference.

00:40:33.589 --> 00:40:36.387
I'm attempting
to lock onto them now, Captain.

00:40:40.163 --> 00:40:41.391
This way.

00:40:58.848 --> 00:40:59.940
Are you all right?

00:40:59.982 --> 00:41:01.415
I am undamaged.

00:41:03.886 --> 00:41:05.877
This was the only way
to the hatch.

00:41:05.922 --> 00:41:07.685
Perhaps there is
another way out.

00:41:10.660 --> 00:41:12.628
There's a hull rupture
in the forward compartment.

00:41:12.662 --> 00:41:14.061
It may provide
a means of escape.

00:41:25.942 --> 00:41:27.204
Start digging.

00:41:32.281 --> 00:41:33.441
Quickly.

00:41:39.956 --> 00:41:42.151
We've disabled
two of their ships.

00:41:42.191 --> 00:41:43.954
The third is still
firing at the surface.

00:41:43.993 --> 00:41:45.984
We're being hailed,
audio only.

00:41:46.062 --> 00:41:50.829
You're committing
an act of war, Captain.

00:41:50.867 --> 00:41:53.392
You've left me no choice,
Councilor.

00:41:53.436 --> 00:41:54.960
Reinforcements are arriving.

00:41:55.004 --> 00:41:56.232
You will be destroyed...

00:41:56.272 --> 00:41:57.398
I don't have time for this.

00:41:57.440 --> 00:41:58.634
Target their weapons array.

00:42:00.341 --> 00:42:01.808
Seven, I need your help.

00:42:31.606 --> 00:42:32.971
I've got them, Captain.

00:42:33.074 --> 00:42:34.405
We're on our way back
to Voyager.

00:42:34.442 --> 00:42:35.841
Acknowledged.

00:42:35.876 --> 00:42:37.036
Good work.

00:42:39.780 --> 00:42:41.839
I'm detecting a fleet
of B'omar vessels approaching.

00:42:41.882 --> 00:42:43.873
68 ships.

00:42:43.918 --> 00:42:47.445
Ensign, as soon as
Mr. Paris's shuttle has docked,

00:42:47.488 --> 00:42:50.321
take us out of B'omar space.
Warp 8.

00:42:50.358 --> 00:42:51.723
Aye, sir.

00:42:54.362 --> 00:42:57.331
Looks like there won't be
any shortcuts this time.

00:43:16.050 --> 00:43:17.540
There you are.

00:43:17.585 --> 00:43:19.610
I wanted to tell you

00:43:19.654 --> 00:43:22.646
that the Doctor said he could
adjust one of your implants

00:43:22.690 --> 00:43:26.285
so that you won't receive
any more homing signals.

00:43:26.327 --> 00:43:27.555
Thank you.

00:43:27.595 --> 00:43:30.587
I hope you don't mind
that I activated this program.

00:43:30.631 --> 00:43:32.531
Not at all.

00:43:34.535 --> 00:43:37.299
I've been thinking
about what you said...

00:43:37.338 --> 00:43:40.796
that this was a place
to encourage your imagination.

00:43:40.841 --> 00:43:43.036
Is that appealing to you?

00:43:45.780 --> 00:43:47.645
I'm not certain.

00:43:50.284 --> 00:43:54.744
I find myself...
constructing scenarios,

00:43:54.789 --> 00:43:57.587
considering alternative
possibilities.

00:43:58.959 --> 00:44:01.928
What if my parents and I
had not encountered the Borg?

00:44:01.962 --> 00:44:04.055
What would our lives have been?

00:44:05.800 --> 00:44:08.928
I would have been raised
by them, learned from them.

00:44:08.969 --> 00:44:12.234
They would have influenced
what I became...

00:44:12.273 --> 00:44:14.173
who and what I am.

00:44:14.208 --> 00:44:19.077
And you... would have done
the same for them.

00:44:19.113 --> 00:44:21.911
If you'd like to know
more about your parents,

00:44:21.949 --> 00:44:25.612
there's information
in the Federation database.

00:44:25.653 --> 00:44:27.280
Information?

00:44:27.321 --> 00:44:30.688
It seems they were
fairly well-known.

00:44:30.725 --> 00:44:32.852
For being unconventional

00:44:32.893 --> 00:44:36.351
and for some rather unique
scientific theories.

00:44:36.397 --> 00:44:39.264
You might like to read
what's there.

00:44:39.300 --> 00:44:43.669
It might...
encourage your imagination.

00:44:45.206 --> 00:44:46.730
Perhaps I will.

00:44:48.476 --> 00:44:49.841
Someday.

00:44:51.679 --> 00:44:52.976
Good night, Captain.
